  "description": "Budget vectors for binary extractor output (plugin-protocol.md section 5.5.5). The budgets are fixed host constants, not negotiated; their names are the BinaryBudget enum. Each case describes one document result: segments is the segment count, text_bytes_each the UTF-8 length of every segment text, and part_chars and locator_chars the character count of every part and locator. A case within every budget is accepted. A case over a budget fails that document with extract-budget (-32010): data.budget names the budget and data.limit holds its value. in-flight is the request-side budget of section 5.5.6 and has no output case here; binary-frames.json uses the same value. The shared validator (slopvac-8l4.20.1) builds each result and replays the file; part and locator cases also agree with the schema pattern bound.",
